      "problem": "Given the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -6 \\\\ \\sqrt{74}\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖2v‖.$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n‖kv‖=|k|\\cdot ‖v‖\n$$\n\nUsing this fact and the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2v‖ & =|2|\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(\\sqrt{74})^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{9+25+36+74} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{144} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
